flowchart TB
accTitle: B3 mandatory protection and bounded singleton or coalition competition
accDescr: B3 admits mandatory candidates first, subject to count, conflict, and capacity constraints. It then compares feasible singleton candidates with complementary coalition proposals under configured size and evaluation limits. A truncated coalition search discards the partial coalition option set and falls back to singleton comparison. The admitted snapshot can still report incomplete coverage or diversity.
    REQ[Validated workspace request] --> MAND[Admit mandatory candidates first]
    MAND --> HARD{Count, conflict, and capacity pass?}
    HARD -->|No| REFUSE[Insufficient mandatory capacity]
    HARD -->|Yes| OPTIONS[Build feasible singleton options]
    OPTIONS --> ENUM[Enumerate complementary coalitions]
    ENUM --> CAP{Coalition search truncated?}
    CAP -->|Yes| FALLBACK[Discard partial coalition choices and use singletons]
    CAP -->|No| COMPARE[Compare singleton and coalition options]
    FALLBACK --> COMPARE_SINGLE[Compare feasible singletons]
    COMPARE --> PICK[Choose best feasible option this round]
    COMPARE_SINGLE --> PICK
    PICK --> MORE{Capacity and slots remain?}
    MORE -->|Yes| OPTIONS
    MORE -->|No| SAVE[Save bounded workspace snapshot]
    SAVE --> STATUS[Report coverage and diversity status]
